---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import ServiceEvidencePanel from '../components/ServiceEvidencePanel.astro';
import serviceEvidence from '../data/serviceEvidence.json';
import LegacyHeader from '../components/LegacyHeader.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactSection from '../components/ContactSection.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ButtonPrimary from '../components/ButtonPrimary.astro';
import ButtonSecondary from '../components/ButtonSecondary.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How is SaaS SEO different from other SEO?',
    answer: "Software buyers need to evaluate fit before committing. Feature, use-case, integration and comparison pages answer different questions, while documentation can serve both prospects and existing users. We choose priorities around the trial, demo or self-serve purchase journey the product actually offers."
  },
  {
    question: 'What results have you achieved for SaaS and software companies?',
    answer: "The football app Search Console screenshot shows 268k clicks for Last 3 months against 200k for Same period last year. These are comparison-period totals, not monthly traffic, signups or revenue. The linked case explains the work and available evidence."
  },
  {
    question: 'Does SEO make sense for SaaS when we already run paid acquisition?',
    answer: "It can, when buyers need product information your current pages do not provide. Compare paid and organic acquisition using your actual signup or demo data. We look for missing comparisons, integration details and use cases before recommending more content."
  },
  {
    question: 'How important is AI search for SaaS companies?',
    answer: "It is worth evaluating alongside organic search when buyers use assistants to compare products. We define the questions, markets and platforms to monitor, check the accuracy of product answers, and separate mentions from referral sessions and verified signups or demos."
  },
  {
    question: 'What is included in a SaaS SEO campaign?',
    answer: 'A defined monthly scope across six workstreams: technical SEO (crawlability, site speed, schema, docs and app-subdomain handling), keyword and funnel research, on-page optimisation, content production or briefs for comparison and use-case pages, authority building through relevant links and digital PR angles, and AI search optimisation. Reporting ties everything to signups and demo requests where tracking allows, not just rankings.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you write comparison and alternative pages?',
    answer: "Yes. We check features, limits, pricing conditions and suitable use cases against current product information. Each comparison should help a buyer choose, including where another product is a better fit. Your product team reviews factual claims before publication."
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does SaaS SEO take to work?',
    answer: "Timing depends on the starting pages, competition, product changes and engineering capacity. We agree release milestones and reporting windows. Click growth in another software case does not set a deadline for demos, activation or lower acquisition costs."
  },
  {
    question: 'How much does SaaS SEO cost?',
    answer: "We scope the work against your product, target customers and website. The proposal separates research, technical implementation, writing, product review and measurement requirements. A small set of comparison pages and a documentation migration need different budgets."
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you work with our product and engineering teams?',
    answer: "Yes. We agree which changes marketing can publish and which require engineering. Technical recommendations identify affected URLs or templates, the proposed change and acceptance checks. Delivery dates are planned around access and your release process."
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you understand product-led growth and freemium funnels?',
    answer: 'Yes. For a self-serve product, we review whether a visitor can understand the offer, start a trial and reach the first useful product action. Public docs, templates and tools may help that journey, but each needs a clear purpose and maintenance owner. We agree how to measure progress from the marketing site into the product, including where tracking is incomplete.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you handle international SEO for SaaS?',
    answer: "We can scope country and language targeting around the markets your product supports. We review regional availability, pricing, integrations and documentation before proposing hreflang or new market pages. Country-level traffic alone does not show that the product can serve those buyers."
  }
];
---

<MainLayout
  title="SaaS SEO Agency | Organic Growth for Software | Bright Forge"
  description="SaaS SEO for product comparisons, integrations and trial journeys. Technical review, product-led content and reporting from our Philippines-based team."
  canonical="https://brightforge.com.ph/saas-seo-services/"
  type="service"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'SaaS SEO Services', item: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/saas-seo-services/' }
      ]
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <LegacyHeader slot="header" />

  <Hero
    badgeIcon="fas fa-rocket"
    badgeText="SaaS SEO Specialists"
    title="SaaS SEO Services for <span>Product Evaluation and Trial Journeys</span>"
    breadcrumbCurrent="SaaS SEO Services"
  >
    <Fragment slot="story">
      <p>We help software teams explain what the product does, who it suits and how to evaluate it. SaaS SEO connects feature, comparison and integration pages with technical work on the marketing site and public documentation.</p>
      <p>We review comparison pages, product facts and the route to a trial or demo. The reporting plan separates search clicks, AI referrals and confirmed product actions so the team can decide which pages need further work.</p>
      <p>Send your product, target customers and trial or demo journey. We will identify the pages to review and the input needed from marketing, product and engineering.</p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <ButtonPrimary href="/contact/" text="Get a SaaS SEO Proposal" />
      <ButtonSecondary href="#saas-results" text="See SaaS Results" />
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="visual">
      <div class="market-visual" aria-label="SaaS SEO growth snapshot">
        <div class="market-node">
          <span>Sports app</span>
          <strong>200k → 268k clicks, three-month year-on-year comparison</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="market-line"></div>
        <div class="market-node forge">
          <span>Fintech SaaS</span>
          <strong>Product facts, eligibility and integration details</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="market-line"></div>
        <div class="market-node">
          <span>Sports SaaS</span>
          <strong>Buyer questions and a route to try the product</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <section class="proof-strip" aria-label="SaaS SEO proof points">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="proof-grid">
        <div><strong>200k → 268k clicks</strong><span>Three-month year-on-year comparison</span></div>
        <div><strong>AI-search review</strong><span>Sessions, mentions and citations</span></div>
        <div><strong>Funnel-led content</strong><span>Comparison, use-case, docs</span></div>
        <div><strong>Engineering-friendly</strong><span>Specs your devs can ship</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="who-for">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who this is for</p>
        <h2>A SaaS SEO agency for teams that need <span>pipeline, not just traffic</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">A buyer comparing software needs more than a feature list: supported workflows, integration requirements, plan limits and a way to test the fit. We review which of those answers are missing before recommending new pages.</p>
        <p>For self-serve products we examine the path into a trial and activation. For sales-led products we focus on the information needed before a useful demo request. Those journeys need different pages and measurement.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid small">
        <article class="card"><h3>B2B SaaS</h3><p>Feature, use-case and comparison pages plus content that reaches decision-makers before your sales team does.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>PLG and freemium products</h3><p>SEO tuned for signups and activation: docs, templates and tools as acquisition surfaces.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Fintech and regulated software</h3><p>Authority-led SEO where trust signals and accuracy matter as much as rankings.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Apps and platforms</h3><p>Consumer and prosumer apps competing for high-volume search demand, like our <a href="/case-studies/football-app-seo/">football app client</a>.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="saas-results">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">Published SaaS results</p>
        <h2>Software search evidence <span>and product review examples</span></h2>
        <p>The football app card shows a Search Console comparison. The AI-search cards are examples of information we would review for those product types, not claims of verified pipeline or completed changes.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="results-grid">
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-tag">Sports App · Team Management</p>
          <h3>+34% comparison-period clicks</h3>
          <p>The screenshot shows 268k clicks for Last 3 months against 200k for Same period last year. Average position moved from 11.4 to 9.1 across the site; the comparison does not establish individual rankings, signups or revenue.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/football-app-seo/">Read the case study →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-tag">Review focus · AI search</p>
          <h3>Fintech: make product limits clear</h3>
          <p>An equity-management buyer needs supported jurisdictions, reporting capabilities and integration requirements. We identify missing information for review by your product and compliance teams.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/ai-fintech-saas-geo/">Related AI-search review →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-tag">Review focus · AI search</p>
          <h3>Sports software: explain the product</h3>
          <p>For team-management software, a buyer needs to compare squad administration, fixtures and reporting. We review whether those tasks have clear pages and a useful route into the product.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/ai-sports-saas-geo/">Related AI-search review →</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="services">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we deliver</p>
        <h2>Full-funnel <span>SEO for software companies</span></h2>
        <p>We choose these workstreams around the product journey and your release capacity. Each needs an implementation owner and a review point.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="service-grid">
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-filter"></i><h3>Funnel &amp; keyword research</h3><p>Problem, solution, comparison and pricing-stage demand mapped to the page types that convert each stage. See <a href="/keyword-research-services/">keyword research</a>.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-balance-scale"></i><h3>Comparison &amp; alternative pages</h3><p>Pages that compare supported features, limits and fit, reviewed against current product information.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-cogs"></i><h3>Technical SEO</h3><p>Crawlability, rendering, schema, docs and subdomain strategy via our <a href="/technical-seo-services-philippines/">technical SEO service</a>: specs your engineers can ship.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-pen-nib"></i><h3>Content production</h3><p>Use-case pages, integration pages and expert-led articles through our <a href="/content-seo-services-philippines/">content SEO service</a>, with factual review by your product specialists.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-link"></i><h3>Authority building</h3><p>Relevant <a href="/backlink-seo-services-philippines/">link building</a> and digital PR angles that make sense for a software brand. No bulk packages.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-robot"></i><h3>AI search optimisation</h3><p>Entity clarity, citable content and measured LLM visibility through our <a href="/ai-search-optimization-services-philippines/">AI search service</a>: with a defined monitoring sample.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-key"></i><h3>Competitor gap analysis</h3><p>Compare rival coverage with your supported features and buyer questions, then prioritise missing pages by relevance and implementation effort.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-chart-line"></i><h3>Signup-led reporting</h3><p>Monthly reports tied to GA4: clicks, signups and demo requests where tracked, work completed, next priorities.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="ai-search">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The AI search shift</p>
        <h2>Make product answers <span>clear enough to check</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">For example, a buyer comparing equity-management software may need to know which jurisdictions and reporting workflows it supports. Those answers need product approval before they become comparison copy or material for AI-search monitoring.</p>
        <p>We record the question, platform and observation date when monitoring answers. If an answer misstates a feature or eligibility rule, we check the source page before recommending a correction. A mention is reported separately from a visit or product action.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timezone-card">
        <h3>What we track for AI visibility</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>LLM referral sessions</strong>: identifiable sessions referred by AI platforms</li>
          <li><strong>Completed actions</strong>: verify the event and destination before counting an enquiry</li>
          <li><strong>Mentions and citations</strong>: where AI platforms name and link your product</li>
          <li><strong>Platform gaps</strong>: where answers omit or misstate product information in the agreed sample</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="process">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">How a campaign runs</p>
        <h2>A delivery sequence for <span>your SaaS SEO campaign</span></h2>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline">
        <article><span>Diagnose</span><h3>Funnel diagnosis</h3><p>Technical audit, funnel-stage keyword mapping, competitor gaps and a priority plan tied to signups, not just traffic.</p></article>
        <article><span>Implement</span><h3>Foundations</h3><p>Technical fixes shipped with your engineers, on-page work on commercial pages, and the comparison-page plan agreed.</p></article>
        <article><span>Publish</span><h3>Content delivery</h3><p>Use-case, comparison and integration pages in production; authority building starts on the terms that matter.</p></article>
        <article><span>Review</span><h3>Review and prioritise</h3><p>Review clicks, signups and AI visibility against the plan, then scale what the data supports.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section faq-section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">SaaS SEO FAQs</p>
        <h2><span>Questions software teams ask</span> before working with us</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="container narrow cta-box">
      <p class="eyebrow">Ready to talk?</p>
      <h2>Get a straight answer about <span>SEO for your product</span></h2>
      <p>Send your website, product documentation and trial or demo path, along with the markets you serve. We can then discuss the missing pages, technical constraints and review work needed for a proposal.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact/" class="cta-primary">Get a SaaS SEO Proposal</a>
        <a href="/case-studies/" class="cta-secondary">View All Case Studies</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ServiceEvidencePanel panel={serviceEvidence['saas-seo-services']} />

  <ContactSection slot="contact" />
  <Footer slot="footer" />
</MainLayout>

<style>
.container {
  width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 2rem));
  margin: 0 auto;
}

.narrow {
  width: min(900px, calc(100% - 2rem));
}

.market-visual {
  position: relative;
  display: grid;
  gap: 1.1rem;
  max-width: 480px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 1.5rem;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.25);
  border-radius: 28px;
  background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(25, 33, 46, 0.09), rgba(25, 33, 46, 0.09));
  box-shadow: 0 25px 80px rgba(25, 33, 46, 0.09);
}

.market-node {
  padding: 1.2rem;
  border-radius: 18px;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  border: 1px solid rgba(25, 33, 46, 0.09);
}

.market-node.forge {
  border-color: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.35);
}

.market-node span {
  display: block;
  color: #b83e12;
  font-size: 0.82rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
}

.market-node strong {
  display: block;
  color: #19212e;
  font-size: 1.05rem;
}

.market-line {
  height: 26px;
  width: 2px;
  background: linear-gradient(#ff6b35, transparent);
  margin-left: 1.2rem;
}

.proof-strip {
  background: #ffffff;
  border-top: 1px solid rgba(25, 33, 46, 0.08);
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(25, 33, 46, 0.08);
  padding: 1.5rem 0;
}

.proof-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 1rem;
}

.proof-grid div {
  padding: 1.1rem;
  border-radius: 16px;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045);
  border: 1px solid rgba(25, 33, 46, 0.08);
}

.proof-grid strong,
.proof-grid span {
  display: block;
}

.proof-grid strong {
  color: #19212e;
  margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
}

.proof-grid span {
  color: #465365;
  font-size: 0.92rem;
}

.section {
  padding: 5.5rem 0;
}

.dark {
  background: #f7f8fa;
}

.darker {
  background: #ffffff;
}

.two-col {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
  gap: 3rem;
  align-items: center;
}

.eyebrow {
  color: #b83e12;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  font-size: 0.82rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
}

h2 {
  color: #19212e;
  font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem);
  line-height: 1.05;
  margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
}

h3 {
  color: #19212e;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}

p,
li {
  color: #465365;
  line-height: 1.75;
}

.lead {
  font-size: 1.15rem;
  color: #465365;
}

.section-head {
  max-width: 820px;
  margin-bottom: 3rem;
}

.centered {
  text-align: center;
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-right: auto;
}

.card-grid,
.service-grid,
.results-grid,
.timeline {
  display: grid;
  gap: 1.25rem;
}

.card-grid.small {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
}

.card,
.service-card,
.result-card,
.timezone-card,
.timeline article,
.faq-item {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.055);
  border: 1px solid rgba(25, 33, 46, 0.09);
  border-radius: 22px;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}

.card a,
.service-card a {
  color: #b83e12;
}

.service-grid {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
}

.service-card i {
  display: inline-grid;
  place-items: center;
  width: 46px;
  height: 46px;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
  border-radius: 14px;
  color: #19212e;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff6b35, #ff9f1c);
}

.results-grid {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
}

.result-tag {
  color: #b83e12;
  font-size: 0.82rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.result-card a {
  display: inline-block;
  margin-top: 0.75rem;
  color: #b83e12;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.timeline {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
}

.timeline span {
  display: inline-block;
  color: #b83e12;
  font-weight: 800;
  margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
}

.timezone-card {
  background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035));
}

.timezone-card ul {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
}

.timezone-card li {
  position: relative;
  padding-left: 1.75rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
}

.timezone-card li::before {
  content: '✓';
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  color: #b83e12;
  font-weight: 800;
}

.faq-section {
  background: #f7f8fa;
}

.faq-list {
  display: grid;
  gap: 1rem;
}

.faq-item summary {
  cursor: pointer;
  color: #19212e;
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 1.08rem;
}

.faq-item p {
  margin-top: 1rem;
}

.cta-section {
  padding: 5rem 0;
  background: #ffffff;
}

.cta-box {
  text-align: center;
  padding: 3rem;
  border-radius: 28px;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.18), rgba(255, 159, 28, 0.08));
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.28);
}

.cta-actions {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 1rem;
  margin-top: 2rem;
}

.cta-primary,
.cta-secondary {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-height: 48px;
  padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem;
  border-radius: 999px;
  font-weight: 800;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.cta-primary {
  color: #0d0f1a;
  background: #fff;
}

.cta-secondary {
  color: #19212e;
  border: 1px solid rgba(25, 33, 46, 0.09);
}

@media (max-width: 980px) {
  .proof-grid,
  .service-grid,
  .timeline {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .results-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .two-col {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .section {
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .proof-grid,
  .service-grid,
  .timeline,
  .card-grid.small {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .cta-box {
    padding: 2rem 1.25rem;
  }
}
</style>
